# AddressSanitizer suppressions for known production bugs in the v0
# prototype. Each entry below corresponds to an issue that the rewrite
# is expected to fix; remove the suppression when the fix lands.
#
# Format: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/AddressSanitizerLeakSanitizer

# --- common/locklessq_v3.hpp:init_ptr leaks block descriptors ------------
# init_ptr() allocates two `locklessq_block_t` with `new` and never frees
# them. There is no destructor on locklessqueue_t_v3 and the queue
# headers are reused for the lifetime of the process in production, so
# the leak does not grow unbounded — but it's still a leak.
# Phase 1 fix: add a destructor (or move ownership to the caller).
leak:locklessqueue_t_v3
